dsh-turn-cost README · Host end: the `turnCost` session projection：- `data.header.config.model` on the `request/header` event decides the current model id; when absent, `default` is used;
- `data.message.id` (or `data.messageId`) on `assistant/message` maintains the
  "assistant message id → turn number" map.

dsh-turn-cost README · The same turn is never counted twice：- a new sample for the same `turn:step` that is **exactly identical** to the previous one → skipped outright
  (this also avoids over-counting "model calls" when the same sample is reported again after a model switch);
- otherwise → the old sample is subtracted first, then the new one is added;
- only a brand-new `turn:step` increments the "model calls" counter by 1.

dsh-turn-cost README · Uninstall：1. Remove the loader entry with `id: turn-cost` from the profile's `cordis.patch.yml`;
2. Delete the plugin directory `…\profiles\node_modules\dsh-turn-cost`;
3. Restart `dsh web`.

The plugin writes no files of its own and has no configuration file of its own, so there is no leftover state
to clean up (the two elements on the page disappear when the page is refreshed).

dsh-turn-cost README · Configuration：- `start < end`: the window is `[start, end)`;
- `start > end`: it wraps around midnight, i.e. `[start, 24) ∪ [0, end)`;
- if `start` / `end` of an entry is not a finite number, that entry is ignored.

When `peakEnabled` is `true` there is one more rule that is easy to trip over: `peakEffectiveAt` must be a
string that **parses into a time**.

dsh-turn-cost README · Testing：- the fallback prices, symbol, decimals, exchange rate and peak switch;
- parsing the configuration from a temporary `ledger.json`, including `decimals` clamping, `exchangeRate`
  fallback, and `peakWindows` wrapping around midnight;
- model price lookup and fallback (model → `prices.default` → fallback price);
- tier selection (peak disabled / before the effective time / inside the peak window / outside it / missing tier);
- the cost formula (four buckets, negatives clamped to 0, invalid rate treated as 1);
- publish fields: package name, absence of `private`, `engines`, `repository`, `files`, and the version matching
  the CHANGELOG heading;
- **the three places the rename must agree**: `name` in `package.json` == `name` in `cordis.patch.yml` == the id
  passed to `window.__ModuleLoader__.load({ id })` in `lib/client.js` (client modules register under that id, and
  a mismatch makes loading fail);
- documentation consistency: every configuration key that is read must appear in both `README.md` and
  `README.en.md`, and the fallback prices and exchange rate in the README must match the code;
